@host = http://localhost:8080
# F5 / dotnet run instead of docker compose? Use the Kestrel port:
# @host = http://localhost:5170

### What is this app running right now (store, cache, discovery, options)?
GET {{host}}/config
Accept: application/json

### Every registered task with its state, priority and next run
GET {{host}}/tasks
Accept: application/json

### Only the scheduled ones (states: Idle, Scheduled, Queued, Running, Completed, Failed, Cancelled)
GET {{host}}/tasks?state=Scheduled&limit=100
Accept: application/json

### A single task
GET {{host}}/tasks/attr:heartbeat
Accept: application/json

### Trigger the manual attribute task (it has no cron string, so this is the only way it runs)
POST {{host}}/tasks/attr:manual/run

### Trigger the manual lambda task
POST {{host}}/tasks/lambda:manual/run

# ─── Execution lock: keepalive, loss, cancellation ──────────────────────────────────────────────

### Keepalive: a 35s run with LockTtl=20s — expect OnLockAcquire, ~3x OnKeepAlive, then OnLockRelease
POST {{host}}/tasks/lock:keepalive/run

### ... watch the lock events
GET {{host}}/activity?take=20&jobId=lock:keepalive
Accept: application/json

### Measured renewal cadence vs. the expected LockTtl/2.
### Set CRONNER_SLOW_KEEPALIVE_MS above LockTtl/2 (e.g. 15000) and run lock:keepalive again:
### the gaps must stay at LockTtl/2, because keepalive hooks are fired detached from the renewal loop.
GET {{host}}/locks
Accept: application/json

### Lock loss, step 1: start the stealable long run
POST {{host}}/tasks/lock:stealable/run

### Lock loss, step 2: steal its claim — the next keepalive fails, the run is cancelled, OnLockLost fires
POST {{host}}/tasks/lock:stealable/steal-lock

### ... watch it stand down
GET {{host}}/activity?take=20&jobId=lock:stealable
Accept: application/json

### Cooperative cancellation: start it ...
POST {{host}}/tasks/cancel:long-runner/run

### ... and cancel it (watch the OnCancel hook in /activity and the logs)
POST {{host}}/tasks/cancel:long-runner/cancel

# ─── Progress reporting ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Live progress, rebuilt purely from the progress hooks (total + per-scope)
GET {{host}}/progress
Accept: application/json

### The progress job's own trace (scopes opening, reporting, closing)
GET {{host}}/activity?take=25&jobId=progress:import
Accept: application/json

### Per-schedule hooks (WithHook<T>, expression hooks, delegate) — only ever fire for this task
GET {{host}}/activity?take=25&jobId=progress:reindex
Accept: application/json

### What the expression-style hooks recorded
GET {{host}}/activity?take=25&jobId=hooks:expression
Accept: application/json

# ─── General observation ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### What the jobs actually did, newest first
GET {{host}}/activity?take=50
Accept: application/json

### Concurrency policies side by side: drop / queue / parallel
GET {{host}}/activity?take=40&jobId=conc:parallel
Accept: application/json

### Hook-fed counters per task, including the lock events
GET {{host}}/metrics
Accept: application/json

### Liveness
GET {{host}}/healthz
Accept: application/json
